Summary: Let Wine's Vulkan find MoltenVK (portability enumeration)
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: gcenx (ported here)
  Commit: 83ca5d2b3104
  URL: https://github.com/Gcenx/macports-wine/blob/fc0301b4896daf29bdf7140d7c67ed01f12aaacd/emulators/wine-devel/files/0001-win32u-Enable-host-Vulkan-portability-enumeration.diff
  File: emulators/wine-devel/files/0001-win32u-Enable-host-Vulkan-portability-enumeration.diff
  Changes: rewritten for Wine 10.0, where winevulkan (not win32u) builds the
    host instance's create info and there's no host_extensions table: a
    helper enumerates the host's instance extensions, and the extension is
    added to the copied list
Upstream: pending (MR !11538; Gcenx, opened 2026-07-31, open on 2026-11-25; not
 in master at 11.22)
Needed until: MR !11538 is merged
Why: MoltenVK is a "portability" Vulkan driver: the Vulkan loader offers it
 only to an instance created with VK_KHR_portability_enumeration and
 VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR. Wine's host instance (built
 by winevulkan in Wine 10.0) asks for neither, so with the loader this project
 bundles (libvulkan.1.dylib) Vulkan has no device. If the host loader offers
 VK_KHR_portability_enumeration, this enables it and sets
 VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR. Sikarugir's 10.0_8 doesn't
 need this: its wrapper supplies MoltenVK as libvulkan.1.dylib, with no
 loader.
Programs: none known; every Vulkan user (DXVK, vkd3d, wined3d's Vulkan
 renderer) would find no device
Seen on: macOS 26.7.2 (a native x86_64 program with the 11.22 build0's bundled
 loader and MoltenVK manifest: vkCreateInstance returns
 VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER without portability enumeration, and finds one
 GPU with it)
References: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11538
Related: ntdll-vulkan-bundled-driver; that one makes the loader find
 MoltenVK's manifest, this one makes it offer the driver
No test: build/smoke.sh's Vulkan step creates an instance and finds a GPU,
 which fails without this

diff --git a/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c b/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c
@@ -635,6 +635,23 @@
  * This function takes care of extensions handled at winevulkan layer, a Wine graphics
  * driver is responsible for handling e.g. surface extensions.
  */
+static BOOL host_has_instance_extension(const char *name)
+{
+    VkExtensionProperties *props;
+    uint32_t count, i;
+    BOOL ret = FALSE;
+
+    if (p_vkEnumerateInstanceExtensionProperties(NULL, &count, NULL) != VK_SUCCESS) return FALSE;
+    if (!(props = malloc(count * sizeof(*props)))) return FALSE;
+    if (p_vkEnumerateInstanceExtensionProperties(NULL, &count, props) == VK_SUCCESS)
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+            if (!strcmp(props[i].extensionName, name)) ret = TRUE;
+    }
+    free(props);
+    return ret;
+}
+
 static VkResult wine_vk_instance_convert_create_info(struct conversion_context *ctx,
         const VkInstanceCreateInfo *src, VkInstanceCreateInfo *dst, struct wine_instance *instance)
 {
@@ -695,7 +712,7 @@
         }
     }
 
-    new_extensions = conversion_context_alloc(ctx, (src->enabledExtensionCount + 2) *
+    new_extensions = conversion_context_alloc(ctx, (src->enabledExtensionCount + 3) *
                                               sizeof(*src->ppEnabledExtensionNames));
     memcpy(new_extensions, src->ppEnabledExtensionNames,
            dst->enabledExtensionCount * sizeof(*dst->ppEnabledExtensionNames));
@@ -723,6 +740,15 @@
         new_extensions[dst->enabledExtensionCount++] = "VK_KHR_external_memory_capabilities";
     }
 
+    if (host_has_instance_extension("VK_KHR_portability_enumeration"))
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < dst->enabledExtensionCount; i++)
+            if (!strcmp(new_extensions[i], "VK_KHR_portability_enumeration")) break;
+        if (i == dst->enabledExtensionCount)
+            new_extensions[dst->enabledExtensionCount++] = "VK_KHR_portability_enumeration";
+        dst->flags |= VK_INSTANCE_CREATE_ENUMERATE_PORTABILITY_BIT_KHR;
+    }
+
     TRACE("Enabled %u instance extensions.\n", dst->enabledExtensionCount);
 
     return VK_SUCCESS;
